{"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK"]]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How a client proves its identity at the token endpoint (RFC 8705 §2, OIDC Core §9 naming)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Only the methods AXIAM actually implements are representable. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"None"},{"type":"text","text":" — the public-client"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"value — was deliberately absent until T21.2: adding it before the rest of the server"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"understood one would have let an operator register a client whose authentication is silently"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"skipped. The server understands one now ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"token.rs"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"authenticate_client_credential"},{"type":"text","text":" has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an arm that accepts "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"no"}]},{"type":"text","text":" credential and refuses a presented one, the authorization endpoint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"derives its PKCE requirement from this enum, and the admin API refuses the method alongside"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"any grant or binding that contradicts it), so the variant exists — and only that arm may"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ever treat a missing credential as success."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ClientAuthMethod"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"open"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" enum. A value this SDK’s copy of the spec does not list decodes to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rather than failing the response it arrived in (CONTRACT.md §27.11 rule 1). Throwing there","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fails the WHOLE response, so one field of one record would take down the page it was on,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"including the records the caller did ask for.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is never read as one of the KNOWN cases: reading a new value as whichever case happens to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"be first turns a new server state into a wrong one, and on this surface these values gate"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"access. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":"’s own raw value is the empty string, which no server value is, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"carrying an unrecognised value back into an update is refused by the server rather than"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"written as a spelling it never used. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"switch"},{"type":"text","text":" over these cases needs an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".unknown"},{"type":"text","text":" arm."}]}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/clientauthmethod"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Enumeration Cases","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientAuthMethod\/clientSecretBasic","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientAuthMethod\/clientSecretPost","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientAuthMethod\/none","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ClientAuthMethod\/privateKeyJWT","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/Ax